WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.867
Now I don’t want to neglect the fact that the

00:00:02.917 --> 00:00:06.950
heart needs its own blood supply to deliver oxygen and glucose.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.321
The heart can receive this blood supply through coronary arteries.

00:00:11.371 --> 00:00:16.950
Coronary arteries branch off the aorta and eventually deliver blood into capillaries.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.950
These capillaries deliver oxygen and glucose to the heart.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.806
Coronary veins will take the deoxygenated blood to the right atrium

00:00:24.856 --> 00:00:28.950
where the blood will eventually travel the pathway to become oxygenated.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:37.315
In fact to quiz yourself, can you pause the video and trace the pathway of blood again?

00:00:37.365 --> 00:00:38.950
Ok, all together.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.950
Right atrium, tricuspid valve, right ventricle, pulmonary valve, pulmonary artery, lungs,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.461
back through the pulmonary vein, left atrium, mitral valve (bicuspid valve),

00:00:50.511 --> 00:00:52.183
left ventricle, aortic valve,

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:55.388
aorta…takes it to the body and then it will eventually

00:00:55.438 --> 00:00:58.950
return through the vena cava back to the right atrium again.
